  ("(1)  Some fruits are masculine: el aguacate ‘avocado’ (la palta south of Ecuador), el albaricoque ‘apri-" 0.0920 0.9080 0.0832 0.0997 0.0997 0.0165 0.00482 0.3431 0.0273 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("cot’, el higo ‘fig’, el limón ‘lemon’, el melón ‘melon’, etc. ‘A banana’ is una banana for most Latin" 0.0920 0.9079 0.0997 0.1162 0.1162 0.0165 0.00482 0.3502 0.0355 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("Americans, but un plátano in some regions and in Spain. Plátano also means ‘plane-tree’ in Spain," 0.0920 0.9081 0.1162 0.1326 0.1326 0.0165 0.00482 0.3536 0.0968 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
