  ("(2)  ’Nuts’ in general are los frutos secos. However, in Latin America las nueces can be used" 0.0920 0.9081 0.1614 0.1778 0.1778 0.0165 0.00482 0.2880 0.0276 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
  ("for  ‘nuts’, cf. cuando está comprando nueces, debe elegir los tipos más populares como almendras," 0.0920 0.9079 0.1779 0.1943 0.1943 0.0163 0.00482 0.2571 0.0247 "UFSJES+Palatino-Italic" 0.0136 nil t 1)
  ("manís, pacanas y nueces de nogal (Colombian cookery book) ‘when buying nuts you should choose" 0.0920 0.9080 0.1944 0.2108 0.2108 0.0165 0.00482 0.3360 0.0524 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("the most popular kinds like almonds, peanuts, pecans and walnuts’. El maní = el cacahuete in" 0.0920 0.9082 0.2109 0.2273 0.2273 0.0165 0.00482 0.3070 0.0269 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("Spain." 0.0920 0.1454 0.2273 0.2438 0.2438 0.0165 0.00482 0.2999 0.0534 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("1.3.4  Masculine by form" 0.0920 0.3731 0.2679 0.2887 0.2887 0.0208 0.00676 0.3763 0.0609 "UFSJES+Univers-Bold" 0.0172 t nil 1)
  ("(a)  Nouns ending in -o are usually masculine: el colegio ‘school’, el libro ‘book’, el macro ‘macro’" 0.0920 0.9080 0.2964 0.3129 0.3129 0.0165 0.00482 0.3375 0.0273 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 1)
