  ("Exceptions: la flor ‘flower’, la labor ‘labour’. El hambre ‘hunger’ is also feminine: see 3.1.2 for an" 0.0920 0.9081 0.5838 0.6003 0.6003 0.0165 0.00482 0.3114 0.0991 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("explanation of the el. Forms like la calor, la color for el calor ‘heat’ and el color ‘colour’ are heard in" 0.0920 0.9080 0.6004 0.6168 0.6168 0.0165 0.00482 0.3075 0.0995 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("regional dialects. Pelambre ‘mop or tuft of hair’ is usually feminine, but sometimes masculine." 0.0920 0.8758 0.6168 0.6333 0.6333 0.0165 0.00482 0.3838 0.0691 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(1) La radio ‘radio’ is feminine in Spain and in the Southern Cone, but in Mexico, Cuba, Central" 0.0920 0.9081 0.6455 0.6620 0.6620 0.0165 0.00482 0.3345 0.0225 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("America and northern parts of South America it is usually, but not always, el radio. In some places" 0.0920 0.9080 0.6620 0.6785 0.6785 0.0165 0.00482 0.3916 0.0726 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("el radio is ‘radio set’ and la radio is ‘radio station’. El radio also everywhere means ‘radius’ and" 0.0920 0.9081 0.6785 0.6950 0.6950 0.0165 0.00482 0.2915 0.0129 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("‘radium’. In García Márquez’s Noticia de un secuestro (Col., 1996) el radio and la radio are used for" 0.0920 0.9080 0.6950 0.7115 0.7115 0.0165 0.00482 0.3415 0.0788 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("‘radio’ with about equal frequency." 0.0920 0.3895 0.7115 0.7280 0.7280 0.0165 0.00482 0.3186 0.0558 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("(2) El porno is masculine even though it comes from la pornografía: detenido T., el rey del porno" 0.0920 0.9080 0.7402 0.7567 0.7567 0.0165 0.00482 0.2816 0.0225 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
  ("español (El Periódico, Sp.) ‘T., king of Spanish porn, arrested’." 0.0920 0.5995 0.7567 0.7732 0.7732 0.0165 0.00482 0.3154 0.0578 "UFSJES+Palatino-Roman" 0.0136 nil nil 0)
